{"id":"49fc4ba1-5704-405c-80da-2f548215d109","object":"chat.completion","created":1784828044,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    if set(core.keys()) != set(nodes):\\n        raise ValueError('core_distance keys mismatch')\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in distances:\\n        if a not in core or b not in core:\\n            raise ValueError('node not in core')\\n        if b < a:\\n            a, b = b, a\\n        w = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        edges.append((w, a, b))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append((a, b, w))\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if n > 1 and len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('graph disconnected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source code for a function solve(case) that computes mutual reachability MST. The function must be self-contained, use only standard library, no external calls.\n\nInput case is a dict with keys: nodes (list of strings), core_distance (dict mapping node to float), distances (list of [node1, node2, float]). Need to compute mutual reachability for each pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then sort edges by mutual reachability value, then by node1 then node2 (canonical order: ensure node1 < node2 lexicographically). Then run Kruskal with union-find (path compression, union by rank). Reject if graph disconnected (i.e., number of edges in MST != len(nodes)-1). Return dict with keys: mst_edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]), total_weight (float). Also possibly include core_distances? The problem says \"Compute core distances, mutual-reachability edge weights, and a deterministic minimum spanning tree\". But core distances are given as input. So output likely includes mst_edges and total_weight. The fixtury shows input shapes only. The registered procedure task DATA-HDB-01. The candidate_artifact mentions \"Return selected edges plus total weight\". So we'll output dict with \"mst_edges\" and \"total_weight\". Also need to validate fields: nodes list, core_distance keys match nodes, distances list with matching nodes.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Build list of all edges: for each distance triple, ensure nodes in canonical order (swap if second < first). Compute weight = max(core[a], core[b], dist). Append (weight, a, b).\n- Sort edges: by weight, then a, then b.\n- Union-Find: parent dict, rank (or size). For each edge in sorted order, if find(a) != find(b), union, add to mst, accumulate total_weight. Stop when mst has n-1 edges.\n- After loop, if len(mst) != n-1, raise ValueError(\"disconnected\").\n- Return dict.\n\nEdge case: duplicate edges? Not given. Distances list should have exactly n*(n-1)/2 entries? Not necessarily, but we process all given.\n\nValidation: nodes list non-empty? Assume at least one node. If no nodes, return? For n=1, MST has 0 edges, total 0. Possibly accept.\n\nImplementation must be exactly Python code string, JSON-escaped.\n\nWrite the code as a string. Then output JSON.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # validate\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    # ensure core keys match nodes\\n    if set(core.keys()) != set(nodes):\\n        raise ValueError('core_distance keys mismatch')\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in distances:\\n        if a not in core or b not in core:\\n            raise ValueError('node not in core')\\n        if b < a:\\n            a, b = b, a\\n        w = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        edges.append((w, a, b))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append((a, b, w))\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1 and n > 1:\\n        raise ValueError('graph disconnected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}\n\nNow we need to JSON-escape: backslashes, newlines, quotes. We'll produce a string with appropriate escapes.\n\nI'll write the code without extra newlines? But need newlines for readability? The JSON string must be a single line with \\n. I'll keep newlines and escape them. Use triple quotes? No, in JSON string we use double quotes and escape.\n\nI'll generate the implementation string carefully.\n\nLet's produce final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1652,"completion_tokens":1594,"total_tokens":3246,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1126},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}